│ during the study. The differences between mean VAS scores at the 2nd and 12th weeks were statistically significant   │
│ in both groups. In conclusion, local steroid injection therapy was found to be as effective as physical therapy for  │
│ the treatment of adhesive capsulitis.Springer"}, {"study_index": 32, "title": "Chapter 12: Interpreting results and  │
│ drawing conclusions", "abstract": "This chapter addresses first one of the key aspects of interpreting findings that │
│ is also fundamental in completing a ‘Summary of findings’ table: the certainty of evidence related to each of the    │
│ outcomes. It then provides a more detailed consideration of issues around applicability and around interpretation of │
│ numerical results, and provides suggestions for presenting authors\' conclusions. Methods are presented for          │
│ computing, presenting and interpreting relative and absolute effects for dichotomous outcome data, including the     │
│ number needed to treat. For continuous outcome measures, review authors can present summary results for studies      │
│ using natural units of measurement or as minimal important differences when all studies use the same scale. When     │
│ studies measure the same construct but with different scales, review authors will need to find a way to interpret    │
│ the standardized mean difference, or to use an alternative effect measure for the meta‐analysis such as the ratio of │
│ means.Wiley Online Library"}, {"study_index": 33, "title": "The painful stiff shoulder", "abstract": "SUMMARY        │
│ This retrospective study of the painful stiff shoulder assesses the response to treatment in 130 patients. Therapy   │
│ consisted of local corticosteroid injections, physiotherapy, or manipulation under anaesthetic. Little difference    │
│ between treatments has been demonstrated, although it seems that early presentation leads to early recovery.         │
│ Oxford University Press"}, {"study_index": 34, "title": "Randomised controlled study of Mulligan\'s vs. Maitland\'s  │
│ mobilization technique in adhesive capsulitis of shoulder joint", "abstract": "Physical therapy is the most          │
│ important part of conservative treatment of frozen shoulder. Both Maitland and Mulligan’s techniques have been found │
